WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.120
Good morning Starshine.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.371
Flower Beauty foam primer, I think yes.

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.960
♪ My money don't jiggle-jiggle, it folds ♪

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.051
Like, how satisfying.

00:00:08.051 --> 00:00:10.070
How to solve any Rubik's cube.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.220
You have the ability

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.640
to influence the world in many ways.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.023
Ways that could be great.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.218
And ways that could be ugly.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.980
Now we see that there's
an ugliness to this,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.530
all I ask is do the right thing, TikTok.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.480
Do the right thing.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.432
TikTok is one of the most
popular social media platforms

00:00:38.432 --> 00:00:40.203
that exists today.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.850
Almost 70% of kids between
the ages of 13 to 17

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.860
are on TikTok on a daily basis,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.230
using it more than all
of those other platforms

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.973
that have existed in our lives.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.850
One of their greatest strengths

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.370
is that it's so popular for kids,

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.793
but that has also become one
of its biggest weaknesses.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.640
Not only do you have some
of the youngest users

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.680
in the world of social media,

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.510
we are also seeing content

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.820
that is proliferating through the app

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.400
that can be potentially harmful to kids.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.920
We're seeing disordered eating content,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.133
we're seeing posts about
suicide and self-harm.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.790
We're also seeing dangerous
and, in some cases,

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.203
deadly challenges.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.430
I'm so protective of the outside.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:39.240
I never thought I'd have to
be protective of the inside.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.030
A social media app.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.220
I never thought in my mind-
Right.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.093
That that could ever result
in me losing my daughter.

00:01:50.203 --> 00:01:55.110
I am here because I don't
want any more children to die,

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.590
I don't want any mother
or father to feel the pain

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.171
and the heartache

00:02:00.171 --> 00:02:04.980
and the brokenness that
we feel every single day.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.600
Because this is hard.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.250
One of the biggest issues
that TikTok is facing today

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.020
is the blackout challenge.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.720
This is a challenge where
children are choking themselves

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.460
until they lose consciousness,

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.040
and then filming the
adrenaline rush they get

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.210
when they wake up.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.280
This game involves individuals

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.113
holding their breath.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.490
We have seen a number of children die

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:32.820
participating in this challenge
across the United States,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.410
and also around the world.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:37.200
Families are suing TikTok
after eight-year-old.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.830
Now, we're seeing lawsuits
being filed against TikTok,

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:44.070
raising the question
of who is responsible,

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:46.023
who is liable for these deaths?

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.560
The only thing that's
certain about this case

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.349
is the incredible opposition
that we're going to face

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:54.840
at every step of the way.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.013
The last thing in the world
these companies want to do

00:02:57.013 --> 00:02:58.914
is stand up in front of a jury

00:02:58.914 --> 00:03:01.855
and explain to them why their
profits were more important

00:03:01.855 --> 00:03:03.153
than life.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.550
Our entire society is bleeding
and our children are dying,

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.220
and unless we do something to change that,

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.170
this is going to keep happening.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.837
My question to TikTok is,
what are you going to do?

00:03:15.837 --> 00:03:18.570
What are you going to do
to change this platform?

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:21.720
Because at this point,
it's not safe for anyone,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.063
and it's definitely
not safe for any child.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.120
For the last 25 years,

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:39.450
my practice has focused
on compensating victims

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:41.763
who are injured by corporate misconduct.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.090
I've recovered over a billion dollars

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:49.050
on behalf of families
who've lost loved ones.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.323
Most of my cases have
involved asbestos victims.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.810
I wanted to do something not
simply to compensate victims,

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.540
but to see if I could use the legal system

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.260
to have less victims in the first place.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.600
Frances Haugen released her papers

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.450
on what the social media companies knew,

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.540
and that reminded me of what
the asbestos companies knew,

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:13.373
only worse.

00:04:13.373 --> 00:04:17.010
The choices being made inside
of Facebook are disastrous,

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.525
for our children, for our public safety,

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.590
for our privacy, and for our democracy.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.200
We can have social media we enjoy.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.300
We can do better.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.280
These companies make
the asbestos companies

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.840
look like choir boys.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.910
These companies know that
children are being injured

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.610
as they speak, right now,

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:36.810
and more importantly,

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:40.650
they continue to target children
through their algorithms.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:43.623
The goal is to addict
children to their products.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.600
Children are being
directed toward material

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.377
that they don't want to see
for purposes of engagement.

00:04:51.377 --> 00:04:53.883
That's what these algorithms
are designed to do.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.620
The Social Media Victims Law
Center is based in Seattle.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.330
It's a small team of lawyers

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.000
that are taking on the biggest
companies in the world.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.540
Filing cases against
social media platforms.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.260
Their cases include suicide on the apps.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.600
Children who have attempted
the blackout challenge

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.070
and tragically died.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.110
Or kids who have been sent down

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:17.790
eating-disordered rabbit holes

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.260
who have ended up in hospital

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.270
over the content that
they have been served

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:23.583
through TikTok and other platforms.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.480
What the center is
really hoping to achieve

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:31.680
is to push social media
companies to accept

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.380
a level of responsibility over these cases

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.283
and put children's best
interests in front of profit.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.280
Corporate misconduct is knowingly putting

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.140
profits over people.

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:49.110
It's knowing that your products hurt kids

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.690
and knowing that you
could make them better,

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:55.500
and intentionally making
the decision not to do so,

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.450
because it would impair their profits.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.253
That to me is corporate misconduct.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:03.450
I think that as long as
you have a profit model

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.433
that is built first,
last and in the middle

00:06:06.433 --> 00:06:09.990
on user engagement above
and beyond all things,

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.420
I think it's inevitable
that you're going to have

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:16.713
these kind of hazards and
these kind of outcomes.

00:06:16.713 --> 00:06:21.000
My clients feel like
if, through this effort,

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.853
one child is saved,
then it's been worth it.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.360
We're in Milwaukee, Wisconsin,

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.040
and I've come down here to talk

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.760
to the family of Arriani Arroyo.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.420
She was a nine-year-old
girl who loved TikTok

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.730
and in February last year,

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:50.010
she was trying the blackout challenge,

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.693
and she tragically died.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:56.010
Earlier this month, July of 2022,

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:59.643
her family filed a wrongful
death lawsuit against TikTok.

00:07:00.874 --> 00:07:03.990
I think the question of
responsibility and liability

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:08.100
of these social media
platforms is a really big one,

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:13.100
and I think this family is
wanting to raise that question.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:17.160
What kind of liability does TikTok have

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.880
when it's young users try
these viral challenges

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.643
and they have fatal consequences?

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:32.060
It seems like a really
nice, quaint, suburban area.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:36.993
It's so sad.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.430
Eggy.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:48.263
Eggy.

00:07:48.263 --> 00:07:49.530
It's time to eat.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.190
Oh, I brought you a napkin.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:54.142
Give me that one.

00:07:54.142 --> 00:07:56.138
Mom, I want a cookie.

00:07:56.138 --> 00:07:58.910
You have that.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.060
Is it warm?

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.179
Mm-hmm.

00:08:01.179 --> 00:08:02.012
Okay.

00:08:02.012 --> 00:08:03.164
That is good.

00:08:03.164 --> 00:08:04.050
Hmm?

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.050
It's good.

00:08:08.768 --> 00:08:11.065
I love you.

00:08:14.858 --> 00:08:15.691
Good boy.

00:08:19.987 --> 00:08:24.450
Arri, she had this
personality that wasn't afraid

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:27.630
to take on the world.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.670
She wasn't afraid to take on a challenge,

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:34.670
she wasn't afraid to do whatever
she felt she wanted to do.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:38.640
Yeah, she loved to sing in her room,

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:42.600
and, I mean, you can hear
her sing out her lungs,

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.660
just singing Alicia Keys,
"This Girl Is On fire".

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.010
That was her song.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:49.300
It was, I mean, over and over,

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:52.650
you could hear her singing her lungs out.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:54.510
She was just so beautiful,

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.070
too beautiful sometimes.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.500
I think we live in such an ugly world

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.783
that she's too beautiful.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:09.016
Why do you think TikTok
was so intriguing to her?

00:09:09.016 --> 00:09:13.170
I go back to the dancing and the singing,

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:15.717
and it was not just that.

00:09:15.717 --> 00:09:18.180
All her friends, all her peers,

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.300
everybody's doing the trends, it's on TV.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.720
TikTok was for everybody, and
it wasn't just a kid thing,

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.840
it was an adult thing,
it was a teenage thing.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.900
I mean, it was just a known app.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.490
She's nine years old.

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:36.570
She's still a little kid and curious.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:41.198
We talked to her many times
before about things like that

00:09:41.198 --> 00:09:44.820
and we've also even warned her of things,

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.310
so we thought we were on great track.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:52.310
It's not something that we
would say would be any harm

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:54.030
or dangerous to her.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:55.180
It's a phone.
Right.

00:09:56.690 --> 00:10:00.750
Do you know, prior to her death,

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.793
how long she'd spend on TikTok?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.280
Every day.

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:06.577
Every single day.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.353
Passionate.

00:10:09.353 --> 00:10:11.790
Don't care about what the
other people say about you.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.350
Be confident and be passionate,

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:16.300
because everyone in this
world is beautiful, so.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:23.760
Social media challenges
really started spreading

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:24.930
throughout the pandemic,

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.328
when kids were unable to be in school,

00:10:27.328 --> 00:10:29.370
they were in isolation at home

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:30.930
and they were turning to social media

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.880
to connect with their peers.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:36.873
And we saw some really
cool challenges pop up.

00:10:39.469 --> 00:10:42.420
But as is always typical
when kids are involved

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:44.280
and when social media is involved,

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:46.980
some of these challenges
started to get edgier,

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.020
they started to get a bit more dangerous.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.935
I was doing the Crate Challenge.

00:10:53.225 --> 00:10:54.654
♪ Left foot, two stomps ♪

00:10:54.654 --> 00:10:56.370
♪ Slide to the left ♪

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:59.507
In January, 2021 we saw the first death

00:10:59.507 --> 00:11:03.030
associated with a challenge
called the blackout challenge.

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:04.680
Individuals holding their breath...

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:08.160
This challenge has existed for decades.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.800
Now we have children
filming themselves doing it

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.140
and it's spreading across social media,

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:15.750
which is encouraging some
of the youngest users

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:18.570
on the platform to try this game

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:23.223
or this challenge without
realizing that it can be deadly.

00:11:25.227 --> 00:11:28.890
This is Arriani right there.

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:30.210
That's her.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.273
I wear this with me on most occasions.

00:11:33.273 --> 00:11:35.820
You think of the happy moments

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.290
you think of the beautiful memories

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:41.550
but the fact that you're never
going to create them again.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.100
We're all just very broken as a family.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:44.933
You know.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.170
Arriani Arroyo was playing

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:50.250
with her four year old brother

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.890
when she accidentally hanged herself.

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:55.080
She'd been asking her parents for months

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.570
to get a dog and they'd finally agreed

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.640
and they'd bought a metal dog leash

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:01.650
to show their children
that they were willing

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.600
to get a puppy.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.520
And Arriani and her brother were playing

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:06.960
with this dog leash.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:08.280
She wrapped it around her neck

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:11.430
and hooked the buckle onto
the hinge of a wardrobe door.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:16.430
She then slipped off a toy
chest and couldn't escape.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:21.390
Their dad then came upstairs
and saw Arriani lifeless.

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:23.070
He called the paramedics

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:27.300
but sadly she never
regained consciousness.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.280
She was buried in a tiara

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:32.463
and a fairy princess dress
with her nails freshly painted.

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:36.810
Her parents believe
that TikTok's algorithm

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:40.323
fed the blackout challenge
to Arriani on her cell phone.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:46.020
We are not living, we are surviving.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.850
Because every day we wake up

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:50.580
and we are not hearing
her say, I love you.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.460
We're not hugging her,
we're not holding her.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:58.020
And anybody that has to go
through what we've experienced

00:12:58.020 --> 00:12:59.520
that's what's going to be the outcome.

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:03.510
And we're here to make sure
that there is education.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:05.100
Where in God's name did you think

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:08.220
that putting a rope around your neck,

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.529
a chain around your neck,

00:13:09.529 --> 00:13:11.883
is something wise to put out there?

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:18.220
And reality is, I feel that like everybody

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:22.533
they should be held
accountable for their actions.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:28.170
My daughter is gone, other kids are gone.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:31.683
There's darker sides to TikTok
than what they're exposing.

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:36.930
Why did you decide that you
wanted to file a lawsuit

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:39.750
against TikTok for wrongful death?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.850
Well, first, yeah, they're responsible.

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:43.800
I feel that they're responsible for it.

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:47.100
Second of all, we need to, right now

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:49.650
we need to save every other
child that's out there.

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:53.820
They need to make changes

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:58.623
because other kids can be
still vulnerable for this.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:06.450
I think it's really important to remember

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.900
that TikTok doesn't want the
blackout challenge to exist

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:10.980
on its platform

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:14.640
and it has taken steps to
try and remove content.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:17.790
So way back in January of 2021

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.130
after the first child's death was linked

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.300
to the blackout challenge

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:23.130
and connected to TikTok,

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.560
the company decided to scrub the ability

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:29.100
to search for blackout
challenge content on the app.

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.077
They have updated their
community guidelines

00:14:31.077 --> 00:14:34.110
to say they ban any kind of content

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:37.320
that glorifies dangerous
or harmful behavior.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:38.604
They've also trained their moderators

00:14:38.604 --> 00:14:41.160
to look out for blackout challenge

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.053
or other dangerous challenges

00:14:42.053 --> 00:14:44.490
that are spreading across their sites.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.440
They are removing this content.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.450
But despite all these safety measures

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.310
the deaths kept happening.

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:53.160
We found that the blackout
challenge was cited

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.290
as the cause of more than a dozen deaths

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:58.500
of children throughout 2021.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:01.050
And I think the biggest legal question

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:03.360
for all of these lawsuits
that we are seeing coming up

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.010
in the courts today is,

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:08.220
can you prove that TikTok's algorithm

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:13.110
sent that blackout challenge
content to the child's phone.

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:15.363
This is her chest where all her,

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.783
some of her stuff,

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:21.393
this is her birth announcement.

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.870
These are her third grade-

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.170
That's right.
Photos.

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:31.110
I know it's been almost two years

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:33.990
but it just still feels like yesterday.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:34.953
It just,

00:15:34.953 --> 00:15:38.280
it's a feeling

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:41.989
that just takes the breath out of you.

00:15:41.989 --> 00:15:44.583
It's a heaviness on your chest.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:49.170
Grief is so hard

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:51.162
and everything I do is just like,

00:15:51.162 --> 00:15:54.659
really reflects off of what I
feel she would want me to do.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:58.360
And I really believe that this fight

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.623
is 'cause that's what
she would want me to do.

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:05.283
And that's why I'm fighting
for her and all these kids.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.963
Because I believe that's
what she would want.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:39.600
So TikTok was created
in 2016 by ByteDance.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.850
A big company based out of China.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.763
It actually took a while
for it to gain traction.

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:48.330
It wasn't until 2018

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:49.838
that TikTok really blew up

00:16:49.838 --> 00:16:52.530
and that was because ByteDance

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:56.040
bought this lip syncing
app called Musically.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:17:00.210
And at the time, musically
had about 200 million users.

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:02.910
Many of these were under the age of 13.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:06.420
This violated the Children's
Online Privacy Protection Act.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.070
Which is a law that says

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:09.689
children under the age of 13,

00:17:09.689 --> 00:17:11.403
you can't collect their data.

00:17:12.933 --> 00:17:16.170
In order to abide by
all of these regulations

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:18.210
TikTok has created a version of its app

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:20.910
in the US that is targeted to kids

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.590
under the age of 13.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:25.590
And it's called TikTok for younger users.

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:29.610
It really tailors the content
to be suitable to kids.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:32.220
And it doesn't target
them with advertising,

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:34.650
but kids know how to get around it.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.650
They just enter the wrong date of birth.

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:43.140
TikTok will tell us that age assurance

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:44.790
is an industry wide issue.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:48.900
But in the last year we've
seen a number of companies

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:52.890
partner with third party
content moderation providers.

00:17:52.890 --> 00:17:54.750
What these providers can do

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:57.992
is run machine learning
age prediction models

00:17:57.992 --> 00:18:01.230
that isn't collecting any
data on the individual.

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:03.360
It doesn't raise privacy concerns

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:06.829
but what it does do is
estimate how old that user is

00:18:06.829 --> 00:18:08.869
and is highly efficient.

00:18:11.254 --> 00:18:14.760
I sent a video of Arriani Arroyo to Hive.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:17.160
This is one of those
artificial intelligence

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:20.580
content moderation companies
that does age prediction

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:24.360
for other big platforms
like Twitter and Reddit.

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:28.350
And it took Hive's technology
three seconds to estimate

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:30.480
that Arriani was 10 years old.

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:33.813
She died just three months
shy of her 10th birthday.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:36.000
TikTok has also met

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:39.300
with these third party
content moderation providers.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:42.720
They ultimately decided not
to deploy this technology

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:43.830
because there were fears.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.050
It could stoke further suspicions

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:48.903
around China spying on young users.

00:18:52.871 --> 00:18:54.530
Wow, okay.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.687
Is that something that you can share?

00:18:56.687 --> 00:18:58.500
What I'd say,

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:01.440
is that the way these
products were designed,

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:04.509
it was impossible for parents to exercise

00:19:04.509 --> 00:19:07.383
meaningful oversight of their children.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:13.410
What's occurring now is
what an economist would call

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:14.820
an externality.

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:17.430
The costs of these unsafe
social media products

00:19:17.430 --> 00:19:19.710
are borne by parents,
they're borne by teachers,

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:21.150
they're borne by law enforcement,

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:23.760
medical providers, psychologists, clergy.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.170
The costs are not being borne

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:27.060
by the entities making the product.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.070
We think that product liability

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:31.020
provides an independent way

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.030
to hold these companies accountable.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:35.820
Not for publishing third party content

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.310
but for designing
algorithms that hurt kids.

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:40.410
If they actually have to pay the cost

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:41.880
of their dangerous products,

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:44.250
they're going to have
the economic incentive

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.503
to design safer products.

00:19:49.392 --> 00:19:52.020
Cars are a lot safer
than they were in 1950.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:54.480
They're a lot more safer
than they were in 1980.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:56.220
And a big reason for that is

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:59.730
that the concept of product
liability creates the incentive

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:02.910
on automobile manufacturers
to think proactively,

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.757
to design safer products.

00:20:04.757 --> 00:20:06.810
And it is our hope

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:08.700
that the same thing can be done here

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:09.707
and that five years from now

00:20:09.707 --> 00:20:13.380
children will be having positive
experiences on social media

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:17.700
and that these horrific
outcomes like Arriani Arroyo

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:18.903
will have stopped.

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:26.146
This whole situation has placed us in a,

00:20:26.146 --> 00:20:27.240
you know,

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.340
everything's almost like red flags.

00:20:29.340 --> 00:20:32.250
You know, Eduardo going to school again.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.540
He's going by himself.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:34.920
It's another thought.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.650
We don't know what the
long term effect is on him.

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.210
You know, you're doing the best you can

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:40.470
and that's all you can do.

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:41.820
That's all you can do.
Yeah.

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:44.760
And you know, we've got
a long road ahead of us

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.130
but we've already made a difference.

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:48.930
And you've already made a difference.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.700
You've already blessed a lot of people

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:51.693
through her memory.

00:20:55.740 --> 00:21:00.300
I think it is the most
innate human emotion,

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:02.130
is protecting your kids.

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:04.200
These were parents that thought

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:05.460
they were doing the right thing.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:06.840
Thought they were being responsible.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:09.690
And then just the profound guilt

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:12.663
that these parents are
feeling is unfathomable.

00:21:13.811 --> 00:21:15.398
♪ Like a highway ♪

00:21:15.398 --> 00:21:17.790
♪ She's living in a
world and it's on fire ♪

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:19.653
Fix the cross and her-

00:21:22.348 --> 00:21:23.181
Yep.

00:21:24.384 --> 00:21:27.040
Hi baby.

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:28.290
That's my baby.

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:32.661
Social media has been designed

00:21:32.661 --> 00:21:34.080
to put things out there

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:36.330
to put content out there,
to make kids believe

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:38.850
that either they're not enough
or they're not good enough.

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:40.983
Or they have to be this way.

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:50.743
♪ In hopes you're on the other side ♪

00:21:50.743 --> 00:21:52.380
♪ Talking to me too ♪

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:53.650
These challenges

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:58.050
I feel just manipulate
the mind to think like,

00:21:58.050 --> 00:21:59.430
if I can conquer this,

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:03.180
if I can do this, you
know, I have purpose.

00:22:03.180 --> 00:22:04.170
You don't need none of that,

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:05.430
to have purpose in life.

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:07.886
We need to, as parents,
remind our children

00:22:07.886 --> 00:22:11.640
what purpose is and and help them

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:14.610
and direct them to finding
their real purpose in life.

00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:16.571
Because social media is not it.

00:22:16.571 --> 00:22:21.571
♪ At night when the
stars light up my room ♪

00:22:22.363 --> 00:22:23.470
♪ I sit by myself ♪

00:22:23.470 --> 00:22:26.493
These social media companies are giant,

00:22:26.493 --> 00:22:29.160
billion dollar Goliaths.

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:32.040
And they will all claim that safety

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:34.110
is their number one priority.

00:22:34.110 --> 00:22:36.450
But when you speak to insiders,

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:38.820
to those who work on
trust and safety teams

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:41.640
tasked with keeping these platforms safe,

00:22:41.640 --> 00:22:43.911
the message I hear time and time again

00:22:43.911 --> 00:22:47.400
is that user safety is not
the number one priority.

00:22:47.400 --> 00:22:49.890
That growth is the number one priority.

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:52.530
Making more money is
the number one priority

00:22:52.530 --> 00:22:53.850
and being the biggest app

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:56.340
in the world is the number one priority.

00:22:56.340 --> 00:22:57.600
That's true of TikTok

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:00.400
and that's true of other
social media platforms as well.

00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:05.940
As we've seen more and
more children be harmed

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:08.551
through social media, we
are now starting to ask

00:23:08.551 --> 00:23:11.490
have these companies been doing enough?

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:15.390
Do they really want to protect
and keep their users safe?

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:17.610
Or are they just doing the bare minimum

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:22.290
to avoid being held liable
against existing privacy laws?

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:25.290
Children have been dying
using these platforms

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:27.840
and these questions aren't going to stop.

